# 18. Cross-agent value-functional narrowness — the Arrow-unique open avenue

Imported verbatim (relative links rebased) from `spikes/PROPOSED-ADVANCED.md` line 110, section *Advanced Mathematical Spike Proposals (detail home) › Phase 3: Surfaced 2026-05-19 (corpus reconciliation scan)*. Not yet re-checked against HEAD: `vsect recheck item:spikes-proposed-advanced-18-cross-agent-value-functional-narrowne-bf71 --outcome holds|stale|landed|not-an-item --why …`.

* **The Gap:** The Arrow charter instance (`#deriv-social-welfare-aggregation-impossibility`) named a structurally unique adjacency: the cardinal-preference escape from IIA is adjacent to `#form-objective-functional`'s value-functional machinery (which carries cardinal value content per sub-agent). The natural extension question — whether the per-sub-agent $V_{O_t^{(i)}}$ canonically lifts to a designer-side cross-agent aggregator (utilitarian summation, weighted utilitarianism, range voting under cardinal-comparability) — is an open framework-scope question raised by Track B's Arrow landing but not engaged at landing. Flagged in `#deriv-social-welfare-aggregation-impossibility` Working Notes (b) as the *robust qualitative* status of the cardinal adjacency; flagged in `#disc-value-functional-grounding-floor` Adjacent Frontiers as the cross-agent narrowness question raised by Arrow.

* **The Spike:** Two structurally distinct branches. (a) **The constructive branch:** does AAT's single-interface commitment of `#form-objective-functional` admit a natural cross-agent lift? Candidates: Harsanyi 1955's utilitarian theorem (von Neumann-Morgenstern utilities + Pareto + impersonality → weighted utilitarian SWF); Sen 1970 §3 cardinal-comparability spectrum (ordinal-no-comparability / cardinal-no-comparability / cardinal-unit-comparability / cardinal-full-comparability); range voting / ratings-based methods as the practical instantiation. If the lift is natural, land as an extension of `#form-objective-functional` carrying the cross-agent aggregator construction. (b) **The no-go branch:** is there a structural reason the value functional's narrowness is *strictly within-agent*, with cross-agent aggregation requiring genuinely new framework machinery (distinct from $V_{O_t}$)? If so, the answer extends the value-functional-grounding cluster to a third charter instance under a cross-agent narrowness reading. Strengthen-first: attempt the constructive branch first; only fall back to the no-go branch if the lift genuinely fails.

* **Honest scope:** Phase-3-grade — open framework-scope question with substantial reach. The constructive branch would extend AAT into the social-welfare-aggregation territory adjacent to `#disc-implementation-impossibility`; the no-go branch would extend the value-functional-grounding-floor cluster's exhaustion claim. Both directions are theory-edge work, likely 3-4 cycles. Most-illuminating open avenue among the three new ADV entries (per the Arrow charter instance's Discussion: this question is "the open avenue most specifically illuminating about how the framework might engage social-choice theory in the future").

